cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ignatiana: A Research Apparatus for the Writings of Ignatius of Loyola"
message: "If you use this apparatus, please cite it as below — and cite the printed edition for any passage you quote."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fassbender
    given-names: Pantaleon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6683-3617"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pantaleonfassbender-coder/ignatian-research"
url: "https://ignatian-research.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A static research apparatus for the six principal works of Ignatius of Loyola:
  a canonical paragraph-level citation index of 1,887 anchors, a concordance
  operating on the reader's own copies, the twenty-four public-domain letters of
  1524-1547 in full, a discernment lexicon, registers of persons and places, and
  a citation-bound dialogue with the corpus. No text of the in-copyright
  translations is distributed.
keywords:
  - Ignatius of Loyola
  - Jesuit studies
  - Spiritual Exercises
  - digital humanities
  - concordance
  - citation index
